From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: defcom5-rockchip <286489597+defcom5-rockchip@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 14:37:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] arm64: dts: rockchip: orangepi-5: source vp0 dclk from
 v0pll; CMA 512M

With FRL-rate modes on the CRU path, rockchip_rk3588_drm_dclk_set_rate()
re-rates the source PLL to the exact pixel clock only when that PLL is
v0pll; gpll/cpll cannot give 1082.89 MHz. Assign dclk_vop0_src to v0pll
as the RK3588 EVB boards do. Also settle the CMA reservation at 512M,
the distribution value (idle use ~11 MB; 4K HEVC 10-bit decode is fine
on 256M).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dts | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dts
index 9e87a97cf288..f4aca35cbb27 100755
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-5.dts
@@ -272,7 +272,7 @@ reserved-memory {
 		cma {
 			compatible = "shared-dma-pool";
 			reusable;
-			size = <0x0 (1024 * 0x100000)>;
+			size = <0x0 (512 * 0x100000)>;
 			linux,cma-default;
 		};
 	};
@@ -1153,6 +1153,17 @@ &vp0 {
 	cursor-win-id=<ROCKCHIP_VOP2_ESMART0>;
 	rockchip,plane-mask = <(1 << ROCKCHIP_VOP2_CLUSTER0 | 1 << ROCKCHIP_VOP2_ESMART0)>;
 	rockchip,primary-plane = <ROCKCHIP_VOP2_CLUSTER0>;
+	/*
+	 * HDMI0 4K@120 runs FRL, where dclk cannot be sourced from the HDMI PHY
+	 * PLL and comes from the CRU instead. rockchip_rk3588_drm_dclk_set_rate()
+	 * only re-rates the source PLL to the exact pixel clock when that PLL is
+	 * v0pll (gpll/cpll are shared and only offer integer dividers), so hang
+	 * dclk_vop0_src off v0pll like the RK3588 EVB HDMI/eDP boards do. Note vp2
+	 * (DP) is on v0pll too (rk3588s.dtsi): a simultaneous DP output would
+	 * contend for the PLL rate.
+	 */
+	assigned-clocks = <&cru DCLK_VOP0_SRC>;
+	assigned-clock-parents = <&cru PLL_V0PLL>;
 };
 
 &vp1 {
